From 2ea81b54a85ae7af8e5adb7abfcf68a034bf7bc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Feb 2026 08:10:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: fix USXGMII RX after speed changes

When transitioning between different USXGMII speeds (e.g., 2.5G to 10G),
the RX path stops working while TX continues to function. The link shows
as UP but no packets are received.

Root cause: phylink only calls pcs_link_up() on speed changes within the
same interface mode, but the Airoha PCS needs full reinitialization to
re-lock the CDR (Clock Data Recovery) to the new line rate.

The fix follows MediaTek's USXGMII PCS driver approach which explicitly
calls the full pcs_config() from pcs_link_up() with the comment:
"Reconfiguring USXGMII to ensure the quality of the RX signal after the
line side link up."

This patch calls data->bringup() instead of data->link_up() for USXGMII
interfaces, ensuring proper CDR calibration and PCS reset on every link-up.
---
 ...iroha-fix-usxgmii-speed-change-issue.patch | 44 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/airoha/patches-6.12/611-net-pcs-airoha-fix-usxgmii-speed-change-issue.patch

diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.12/611-net-pcs-airoha-fix-usxgmii-speed-change-issue.patch b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.12/611-net-pcs-airoha-fix-usxgmii-speed-change-issue.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000000..58a6e10dd2e43b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.12/611-net-pcs-airoha-fix-usxgmii-speed-change-issue.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+From: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 01 Feb 2026 08:00:00 -0600
+Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: fix USXGMII RX path after speed changes
+
+When transitioning between different USXGMII speeds (e.g., from 2.5G to 10G),
+the RX path is not properly reinitialized, causing the link to show as UP
+but no packets are received.
+
+The root cause is that phylink only calls pcs_link_up() when speed changes
+within the same interface mode (USXGMII), but the Airoha PCS requires a full
+reinitialization to properly lock the CDR (Clock Data Recovery) to the new
+line rate.
+
+Fix this by calling data->bringup() instead of data->link_up() for USXGMII
+and 10GBASER interfaces in the pcs_link_up callback. This ensures the full
+PCS initialization sequence is performed, including CDR calibration and
+global reset, similar to MediaTek's USXGMII PCS driver which calls the full
+pcs_config() from pcs_link_up().
+
+Signed-off-by: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
+---
+ drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c | 12 ++++++++++--
+ 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
++++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+@@ -768,8 +768,16 @@
+ 		}
+ 	}
+
+-	if (data->link_up)
++	/* For USXGMII/10GBASER, reconfigure the PCS to ensure RX signal quality
++	 * after link up, similar to MediaTek's USXGMII PCS driver.
++	 * This is required when speed changes within the same interface mode.
++	 */
++	if ((interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII ||
++	     interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10GBASER) && data->bringup) {
++		data->bringup(priv, interface);
++	} else if (data->link_up) {
+ 		data->link_up(priv);
++	}
+
+ 	/* BPI BMI enable */
+ 	regmap_clear_bits(priv->xfi_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_GIB_CFG,
